        <CheatEntry>
          <ID>9</ID>
          <Description>"Infinite Usable Items"</Description>
          <VariableType>Auto Assembler Script</VariableType>
          <AssemblerScript>[ENABLE]
aobscanmodule(ActR_ItemManager_AddItem,GameAssembly.dll,48 89 7C 24 20 41 57 48 83 EC 20 80 3D 74 C3 78 00 00 44 8B FA 48 63 F9 75 12 8B 0D 34 25 33 00)
alloc(ActR_ItemManager_AddItemCode,128,ActR_ItemManager_AddItem)
label(ActR_ItemManager_AddItemOriginal)
label(ActR_ItemManager_AddItemReturn)

ActR_ItemManager_AddItemCode:
  // ItemManager.AddItem(id, delta): retain normal pickups and resource handling.
  cmp ecx,FFFFFFFF
  je ActR_ItemManager_AddItemOriginal
  test edx,edx
  jns ActR_ItemManager_AddItemOriginal

  // Normal inventory item with a negative delta: consume zero instead.
  xor edx,edx

ActR_ItemManager_AddItemOriginal:
  mov [rsp+20],rdi
  jmp ActR_ItemManager_AddItemReturn

assert(ActR_ItemManager_AddItem,48 89 7C 24 20)
ActR_ItemManager_AddItem:
  jmp ActR_ItemManager_AddItemCode
ActR_ItemManager_AddItemReturn:

registersymbol(ActR_ItemManager_AddItem)

[DISABLE]
ActR_ItemManager_AddItem:
  db 48 89 7C 24 20

unregistersymbol(ActR_ItemManager_AddItem)
dealloc(ActR_ItemManager_AddItemCode)
</AssemblerScript>
        </CheatEntry>
      </CheatEntries>
    </CheatEntry>
  </CheatEntries>
  <UserdefinedSymbols/>
  <Comments>Actraiser Renaissance (Steam/PC)
Includes separate script groups for Act Mode / side-scroller gameplay and Settlement / Angel Mode.

Act Mode Infinite HP captures the exact live player parameter-block pointer during ActlReadObject.CallFixedUpdate, then filters the authoritative shared SVObjParamater.Damage routine by pointer identity. Infinite MP uses unique GameAssembly.dll AOB signatures derived from the game's IL2CPP MP accessors. Infinite Lives keeps SaveData.actContinueCnt (continues used) at zero; zero corresponds to the displayed three lives.

Settlement / Angel Mode Infinite HP and Infinite SP hook the angel-specific CRTAngel setters and replace attempted changes with the live maxHp or maxSp field. Angel SP Value = 90 keeps both the saved value and visible HUD counter at 90 while enabled and restores its previous saved value when disabled. It is compatible with Infinite Angel SP.

Max Realm Resources keeps the active realm's material/resource counter at 999 and synchronizes its HUD display. Infinite Usable Items prevents negative ItemManager quantity changes for normal inventory IDs while preserving pickups and the separate realm-resource ID. These scripts do not touch enemy or Act Mode health routines.

Attach Cheat Engine to ActraiserR.exe, expand the group, and activate entries individually.</Comments>
</CheatTable>
